zjd|n|The act of igniting, kindling, or setting on fire. ; The state of being ignited or kindled.	N:2168,62,4~2168,62,4
zjw|v|To be ignorant of or not acquainted with. ; To throw out or reject as false or ungrounded; -- said of a bill rejected by a grand jury for want of evidence. See Ignoramus. ; Hence: To refuse to take notice of; to shut the eyes to; not to recognize; to disregard willfully and causelessly; as, to ignore certain facts; to ignore the presence of an objectionable person.	d:1431,37,5~1431,37,5
